  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Resilient, Adaptive and Disaster-Ready Communities in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">- To use the planning grant provided to develop a full proposal to be funded by Visa Corp. for 5 years.  - This will involve:       Holding consultations with Asal Humanitarian Network (AHN) partners to socialize the concept of Anticipatory Action and the necessary Digital Financial Inclusion, to identify likely partners (civil society, government, financial service institutions and tech partners, scientific organizations), develop the national Building Resilient, Adaptive and Disaster Ready Communities (B -READY) project objectives, activities, and ways of working, and develop country -level B -READY implementation proposals      Commissioning a scoping study to ascertain the priority hazards, counties/sub -geographies and target populations to be supported during the full project implementation.      Holding partner  -level consultations to agree on the budget, Monitoring, Evaluation and Accountability and Learning (MEAL) framework and indicators for the full proposal.      Holding workshops with Oxfam America and colleagues from other implementing countries e.g., Philippines, Vietnam, Lebanon and the United States (US) (Puerto Rico) validate the developed proposal.</narrative>
  </description>
